                    {
                        "sense_id": "f8ee1de2-59ed-3e0e-909d-822cd6d4ea55",
                        "entry_id": "519f6048-1b29-3a1d-b72d-0ad5a0bdbc4f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who suffers; one who is afflicted."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea40deb3-31c3-4fa3-9664-7c8553a2578c",
                                "sense_id": "f8ee1de2-59ed-3e0e-909d-822cd6d4ea55",
                                "text": "All the main-line railways, as well as London Transport, were affected by flying-bomb damage, but naturally the Southern Railway was the principal sufferer for geographical reasons, and the L.N.E.R. came next with the damage it sustained in the Stratford area."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cbdccdd9-de64-3ee1-aff7-9aa5e4e7d7c9",
                        "entry_id": "519f6048-1b29-3a1d-b72d-0ad5a0bdbc4f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tailor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "obsolete",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e491e87-633f-4b3a-a26c-de58ff770f6d",
                                "sense_id": "cbdccdd9-de64-3ee1-aff7-9aa5e4e7d7c9",
                                "text": "From a creditor, being a \"victim,\" \"schneider,\" \"sufferer,\" or \"tailor,\" to one who sets off his wares by wearing the same, being consequently a debtor. HONOURED SIR,— I can scarcely express my delight at your kind compliments as to the fit and patterns […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
